From e02cd914fbdfbcc7659dfc5843b69d50d7319a81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:17:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] expert-cache: the streamed prefill and the dynamic hot slots
 read kt-kernel's MXFP4 expert cache

With KT_MXFP4_EXPERT_CACHE_GIB (kt-kernel-expert-cache.patch) the routed experts live in a RAM cache
of fixed slots instead of arenas holding all of them, so V4.1-1017 runs on one socket with 256 GB.

- kt_stream_prefill: the cache's memfd is mapped and registered as pinned; a group's cached experts
  are copied from their slots, the others are read from the checkpoint (O_DIRECT,
  KT_MXFP4_STREAM_READERS threads) into a pinned bounce first. The ue8m0 scale bytes are widened
  to the fp32 scales the regroup reads on the GPU (e << 23).
- kt_kv_hot_lend: a swapped-in expert is copied from its cache slot, which stays pinned in the
  cache until the copy is done, or read from the checkpoint when the cache does not hold it.
- KT_MXFP4_STREAM_REPORT: the cache counters every that many streamed layers (40).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYXChrDp1ydY24uuGvf2k2
